'''Pawp''' was a [[video store]] on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]] during the [[Clone Wars]]. Billboards were put up in order to advertise the business. One particular billboard, [[Writing|written]] in [[Aurebesh]] characters, read "VIDEO STORE" - "PAWP". The business' logo showed the last character upside-down.<ref name="Sabotage">{{TCW|Sabotage (episode)}}</ref> Another Pawp store was located in the [[city]] of [[Ro Station]] on [[Pantora]].<ref name="Cornered">{{TBB|Cornered}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Pawp is introduced in the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' episode "[[Sabotage (episode)|Sabotage]]." However, concept art for the show reveals that the business was originally created for the episode "[[To Catch a Jedi]]," where Pawp was going to be a pawn shop known as "Pawn."<ref name="TCAJ Concept Art">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/to-catch-a-jedi-concept-art-gallery|text="To Catch a Jedi" Concept Art Gallery}} {{C|Slide 6}}</ref>

